Seam: BrowserNativeWidgetMac::GetWindowFrameTitlebarHeight.
Why: Arcium hides the tab strip and the toolbar, so upstream's height comes
     out near zero and macOS puts the traffic lights hard against the top of
     the window, above the nav row they sit beside. AppKit centres those
     buttons in the title bar, so the window needs a height that centres them
     on the nav row instead.
Delegates to: BrowserSidebarController::TitlebarHeight

